{"availability":"available","full":"jbikker/tinybvh","name":"tinybvh","description":"Header-only dependency-free BVH construction and traversal library.","category":"Other","language":"C++","stars":1225,"forks":84,"created":"2024-10-29T14:51:23Z","updated":"2026-10-16T20:44:23Z","license":"MIT","branch":"main","homepage":"https://jacco.ompf2.com/2025/01/24/tinybvh-manual-basic-use/","topics":["bvh","raytracing","rendering"],"demo":"https://electronicarts.github.io/gigi/Demos/tinybvh/index.html","color":"#323057","ink":"#d6caff","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-19T11:46:37.219Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-19T11:46:37.219Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-19T11:46:37.219Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-09T23:11:40.192Z","stars":1210,"forks":82},{"at":"2026-10-15T12:58:17.800Z","stars":1224,"forks":82},{"at":"2026-10-19T11:46:37.219Z","stars":1225,"forks":84}],"technologies":[],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["Header-only BVH construction and traversal library written in C++14 / \"Sane C++\" (or \"C with classes\"). C++17 is used for threading. This library has no dependencies.","TinyBVH is fast. Here is, in a nutshell, how it compares to Intel's Embree and Madmann91's BVH library. TinyBVH currently builds a SAH BVH faster than Embree and Madmann91. It also traces individual primary and 'any hit' rays faster than those libraries. Note: These results are based on the new tinybvhbenchmark.cpp application and are cautiously presented as 'preliminary'. Single-ray traversal is only a small part of Embree. If you suspect an imperfection in the experiment setup, please let me know. When tracing rays on the GPU, (multicore) CPU performance is dwarfed. On an RTX 5080 laptop…"],"features":[],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/jbikker/tinybvh/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"0a0833dd588a97225562215216610c9ccb3266a01b85aa51a2dc6b55ef35392a","extractedAt":"2026-10-09T23:11:40.292Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-09T23:11:40.292Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text